EA = (f"Purpose: This study examines how time-budget pressure and organisational ethical climate affect auditors' silence about a detected irregularity through moral disengagement, and whether professional conscience weakens this process. "
      f"Design/methodology/approach: A survey of {n} auditors working in the Audit Organization and audit firms was analysed with covariance-based structural equation modelling using fully latent variables (no item composites), two latent interaction terms and {R['boot_n']:,} bootstrap draws. "
      f"Findings: Time-budget pressure increased moral disengagement (β = {PA['MD~TBP']['beta']:.2f}) and ethical climate reduced it (β = {PA['MD~ECL']['beta']:.2f}). Moral disengagement was the strongest predictor of silence (β = {PA['SIL~MD']['beta']:.2f}); ethical climate also had a direct negative effect on silence (β = {PA['SIL~ECL']['beta']:.2f}), while the direct effect of time pressure was not significant, which indicates that it works mainly through justification. Professional conscience weakened both the effect of time pressure on moral disengagement (β = {PA['MD~INTT']['beta']:.2f}) and the effect of moral disengagement on silence (β = {PA['SIL~INTM']['beta']:.2f}); the indirect effect of time pressure on silence fell from {IN['TBP_MD_SIL_low']['est']:.2f} at low conscience to {IN['TBP_MD_SIL_high']['est']:.2f} at high conscience. The model explained {R['r2']['SIL']*100:.0f}% of the variance in silence. Results were stable across DWLS estimation, residual-centred product indicators, a respecified model and outlier trimming; a reverse-path model fitted almost equally well, so the causal direction rests on theory. "
      f"Originality/value: The study treats silence as the end point of a chain of pressure, justification and silence, and shows that organisational climate and internalised professional values act on different links of this chain. "
      f"Practical implications: Protected time for unusual findings, training that makes justification mechanisms visible, ethical leadership and safe channels for raising concerns are likely to reduce silence more effectively than exhortation to report.")
ewc = len(re.findall(r"\S+", EA)); print("EN abstract words", ewc); assert 200 <= ewc <= 330, ewc
d.para("**Abstract:** " + EA, jc="both", indent=False, size=18, rtl=False, persian=False, after=60)
d.para("**Keywords:** Ethical climate, Auditing, Moral disengagement, Silence, Time-budget pressure, Professional conscience", jc="left", indent=False, size=16, rtl=False, persian=False, after=0)
d.save(os.path.join(DEL, "Paper_FA_Auditor_Silence.docx"))
print("saved")
